{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git show 398775c'","aggregated_output":"commit 398775c32bf960715ac3a791d1f6aca9f9183d3b\nAuthor: Stuart Bowness <1020179+stuartbowness@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri May 1 06:52:35 2026 -0700\n\n    [task-4] fix: replace awkward 'check each/every check' with 'verify'\n\ndiff --git a/skills/mission/SKILL.md b/skills/mission/SKILL.md\nindex 4010def..6f3a8c5 100644\n--- a/skills/mission/SKILL.md\n+++ b/skills/mission/SKILL.md\n@@ -348,7 +348,7 @@ Create `contract.md` in the change directory (`openspec/changes/<change-name>/co\n 1. Group checks by task, matching the task list in tasks.md.\n 2. Checks should describe **observable behavior** verifiable from outside the code (HTTP response, CLI output, file on disk, UI state, build passing, etc.). Where this is genuinely not possible, use `[inspection]` checks -- see the verification method tags in the contract template for caps.\n 3. Do NOT reference implementation details (function names, variable names, internal data structures).\n-4. Be specific and unambiguous. A validator reading only the contract and the diff should be able to check every check without guessing.\n+4. Be specific and unambiguous. A validator reading only the contract and the diff should be able to verify every check without guessing.\n 5. Workers never see this file.\n 6. **Write the minimum set of checks needed to verify the task is complete and correct.** Each check should trace to a specific spec scenario (e.g., `add-todo/1`), including error behaviors specified in the specs. Do not add checks for edge cases, nice-to-haves, or defensive behaviors unless the PRD explicitly requires them. If a check would not cause you to reject the task when it fails, do not include it. Place checks on the earliest task where they become verifiable -- if a behavior spans multiple tasks, put the check on the task where it can first be checked, not where the work begins.\n \ndiff --git a/skills/mission/prompts/usertest-validator.md b/skills/mission/prompts/usertest-validator.md\nindex 31db48a..18049b2 100644\n--- a/skills/mission/prompts/usertest-validator.md\n+++ b/skills/mission/prompts/usertest-validator.md\n@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ SHA: <commit-sha>\n    - **Both backend and frontend**: Run HTTP tests first, then /test-app for the UI.\n    - **Infrastructure only** (config, build, CI): Verify the build passes and config is correct. You may mark behavioral checks as SKIP with reason \"infrastructure-only change, not testable via HTTP or browser.\"\n \n-3. **Check each contract check:** For each check, run the appropriate test. Mark PASS, FAIL, or SKIP.\n+3. **Verify each contract check:** For each check, run the appropriate test. Mark PASS, FAIL, or SKIP.\n    - PASS: The check is demonstrably true.\n    - FAIL: The check is demonstrably false, or the test reveals a bug.\n    - SKIP: The check cannot be tested from outside (e.g., internal refactor) or the work is deferred to a later task. Provide a reason. If deferred to a later task, append to `mission/deferrals.md` as `task N -- <check>`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
